# mobile-app/.env.example — the ONE mobile environment template.
#
# Copy to `mobile-app/.env` (git-ignored). Everything here is public by
# design: EXPO_PUBLIC_* values are embedded in the app bundle, so a secret
# must NEVER live in one — RLS is the authority for the public anon key.
#
# The client is wired in src/lib/supabase.ts; M1 ships without auth, so an
# unconfigured build renders the honest "Not configured" state on More.

# The Supabase project URL (local stack default: http://127.0.0.1:54937 on
# this host; a device reaches it only through adb reverse or a LAN address —
# see mobile-app/README.md).
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=

# The public anon key (never the service-role key).
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Dev/preview only: allow cleartext HTTP so a device can reach a local
# server. Unset in production builds (HTTPS only).
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ALLOW_CLEARTEXT=
# The UniPilot web server the app calls for WhatsApp groups (Bearer API, plan B.1 channel iii).
# Public by design (a URL, never a secret). Local: http://127.0.0.1:3000 with adb reverse tcp:3000 tcp:3000
# (needs EXPO_PUBLIC_ALLOW_CLEARTEXT=1); production: the HTTPS origin. Unset = the screen says so.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=
